me `LANG`, `LANGUAGE=`, `LC_MESSAGES` and `FORMAT_VARS` lines in `control/environment`; *Language & Region* sets the system's with `localectl set-locale` (trixie's localed can) and generates a missing locale through the helper's `locale-add` (`/etc/locale.gen`, `locale-gen --keep-existing`). Night light (`night-light.enabled`, default on, `night-light.temperature` = wlsunset `-t`; on *Displays*): autostart runs `flickos-control night-light` (execs flickos-settings' `night-light` script, which passes options to wlsunset, with `FLICKOS_NIGHT_LIGHT=1`; nothing while off), a change restarts only FlickOS's wlsunset. Do Not Disturb (`notifications.do-not-disturb`, *Notifications* page) is mako's `do-not-disturb` mode from flickos-settings' mako config (critical still shown); `makoctl` runs only while the user's mako owns `org.freedesktop.Notifications` (mako's D-Bus activation would start a plain mako), and autostart's `flickos-control notifications` re-adds the mode after login when on. Startup applications (*Startup Applications*, `flickos-control startup list|enable|disable|add|remove|run`): XDG autostart by the spec (user folder first, `Hidden`, `OnlyShowIn`, `TryExec`, `Exec` field codes, `X-GNOME-Autostart-enabled=false` = off, a system entry changed through a user copy); autostart runs `startup run` last (waits ≤10 s for the tray); flickos-settings' `/etc/xdg/flickos/autostart` hides the entries of what its autostart starts itself and keeps the print applet off, so nothing new starts by default. Automatic updates (*Updates*, installed only; `flickos-control updates` prints them) are read from `apt-config dump`; the helper's `updates auto|scope|reboot VALUE` writes `/etc/apt/apt.conf.d/60flickos-updates` (`#clear`s the origins; scopes `UPDATE_SCOPES` in both files). flickos-settings Breaks flickos-control (<< 1.10). *Displays* keeps screen arrangements: `flickos-control displays list|save|forget|start` writes one kanshi profile per set of connected screens (`wlr-randr --json`) into `~/.config/flickos/displays`; autostart's `displays start` execs kanshi with `FLICKOS_DISPLAYS=1` only while one is kept and no other kanshi runs, and `save`/`forget` SIGHUP, start or stop it (Depends kanshi, wlr-randr). *Default Applications* runs `flickos-control default-app set` (`xdg-mime default`, or `~/.config/xdg-terminals.list` for the terminal); Super+Enter/the menu run `xdg-terminal-exec` (FlickOS default foot in flickos-settings' `/etc/xdg/flickos/xdg-terminals.list`), Super+B/Super+E/the menu run flickos-settings' `/usr/libexec/flickos/open-default browser|files`. *Date & Time* runs `timedatectl` (flickos-desktop depends on `systemd-timesyncd`; systemd only recommends it). *Login* (installed systems with flickos-greeter's `autologin` group only) runs the helper's `autologin-on`/`autologin-off`, for the calling user only (`PKEXEC_UID`). *Users* (installed systems only) runs its `user-add NAME FULLNAME yes|no`, `user-remove NAME keep|delete`, `user-admin NAME yes|no`, `user-password NAME` (passwords on stdin; adduser/chpasswd/userdel/gpasswd; administrators = group `sudo`; new accounts get the installer's `defaultGroups`, `DEFAULT_GROUPS`; never the caller's account, a logged-in one or the last administrator). *Firewall* (while `/etc/ufw/ufw.conf` exists; ufw is only a Recommends of flickos-desktop) reads its `ENABLED=` (world-readable; `ufw status` needs root) and runs the helper's `firewall-on`/`firewall-off` (`ufw --force enable`/`ufw disable`); rules stay `sudo ufw`. *Phone* (Devices group; while flickos-phone is installed, not with `boot=live`) owns no settings: it reads one `flickos-phone state` (again every `PHONE_REFRESH_SECONDS` while mapped, the timer stops when it isn't), runs `flickos-phone set|forget|network`, and *Add Phone…* talks to `flickos-phone pair --json` (events on stdout, yes/no on stdin; Cancel before a request kills it, which closes the daemon's pair window). Its firewall row is the system setting `firewall.phones`