`id` (ns). Add a `HISTORY_LABELS` entry (and `can_undo`/`undo_commands` for a new owner, `SYSTEM_LABELS`/`check_system`/`system_value`/`system_command` for a new system setting) when adding a setting. Pages whose class has `available()` false are left out. *About* (`system_info()`; `flickos-control about` prints it plus FlickOS's package versions, for bug reports) copies with `wl-copy`. The sidebar groups the pages under headings (`Page.group`; `PAGES`/`PAGE_CLASSES` in sidebar order, a group's pages together: Desktop layout, tiling, notifications; Devices displays, input, keyboard, shortcuts, idle; Apps apps, startup; System region, datetime, memory, updates; Accounts and security users, login, firewall; then history, more, about with no heading) in a `GtkListBox` (`page_list()`; `GtkStackSidebar` has no headings). Other pages own no settings: they run the owning command (`flickos-layout`, `flick-tiler`, `flickos-shortcuts`); constructors only build widgets, and `shown()` reads through `Ui.background()` (a thread, newest answer per key wins, spinner until then) so the window opens at once; the layout page reads everything with one `flickos-layout state` (JSON, flickos-layouts >= 1.19); changes run with `run_async`; a missing capability goes into the owner (hence `flick-tiler floating list|add|remove`, `gap N`, and `ratio`/`gap` in its status, flick-tiler >= 1.3). *More Settings* tiles (`TILES`, same apps as the Settings menu, plus Hello, which owns a setting in its own window) are hidden when the app is missing. Search box above the pages: `Ui.row()`/`Ui.heading()` index what pages build while the window opens (`ui.indexing`), plus pages, tiles and `SEARCH_KEYWORDS` (one entry per page and tile, a test checks); `find` folds case and accents; a result scrolls to the row and focuses its control, or starts the tile's app. Add keywords when adding a page or tile. One window per session (`control.lock`). Design, ADRs and the phase plan (input, keyboard layout, idle, login next): `docs/design/flickos-control.md`. Unit tests in `tests/`. A Depends of flickos-desktop and in `REQUIRED`.
+  - `flickos-hello`: the example program (`usr/bin/flickos-hello`, single Python 3 file, GTK 3 via python3-gi only for `show`; design: `docs/design/flickos-hello.md`). Owns the greeting (`GREETINGS`, `flickos-hello greeting list|current|set ID|default`; conffile `/etc/xdg/flickos/hello.conf` `[Hello] Greeting=`, then `~/.config/flickos/hello`; 1.x's texts still read). `say [NAME]` prints it; `show` is a window with the greeting and a list, one per session (`hello.lock`). `record()` for History (`HELLO` in flickos-control, undo = `greeting set OLD`); a *More Settings* tile in flickos-control (INT-4), not in the Settings menu. A **Recommends** of flickos-desktop (an app users may remove; new installs only), not in `REQUIRED`. Unit tests in `tests/`.
   - `waypaper`: upstream waypaper (GPL-3+, not in trixie) installed as is, version `X.Y+flickosN`, plus FlickOS defaults in `/etc/xdg/waypaper/config.ini` (read by a patched `config.py`). A Depends of flickos-desktop.
   - `sfwbar`: upstream sfwbar (GPL-3, a GTK 3 layer-shell panel/dock; Debian dropped it), vendored at a git commit after 1.0_beta17 (beta17 lacks taskbar `pins` and breaks `size = "auto"`), version `1.0~betaN+gitYYYYMMDD+flickosN`. The only compiled package: `Architecture: any`, meson via `debian/rules` with optional features set explicitly, no -dbgsym. FlickOS patches (`FlickOS:` comments, listed in `debian/README.source`): the `running` CSS class on an app's dock button, and the bar property `sensor_maximized` (hide only while the focused window is maximized/fullscreen on the bar's output; needs window state changes to call `wintree_commit`). The Cupertino layout's dock (`sensor`, `sensor_maximized`, `exclusive_zone = "0"`) and Traditional's bottom panel (taskbar in an `hscroll` grid so it never pushes the pager off; pager of labwc's ext-workspace desktops, `workspace_mod_state` FlickOS fix so the current one is `focused`); a Depends of flickos-layouts.
