+### `flickos-hello`
+
+The example program: it says hello with the greeting the user chooses, and
+shows every part of a FlickOS program in about 430 lines (a setting with a
+system default and a user choice, the command line, a window, History, tests,
+a desktop file). Design: [flickos-hello](design/flickos-hello.md). One Python 3
+file, `usr/bin/flickos-hello`, GTK 3 through python3-gi for the window only.
+
+- **The setting:** the greeting, one of `GREETINGS` (id, text).
+  `flickos-hello greeting list|current|set ID|default`; the default for every
+  account in the conffile `/etc/xdg/flickos/hello.conf` (`[Hello]
+  Greeting=`), a user's choice in `~/.config/flickos/hello`. A broken file or
+  an unknown greeting is a warning, never an error. 1.x's texts (`Hello`)
+  are still understood.
+- **The window** (`flickos-hello show`, *Hello* in the app list and on
+  *Settings → More Settings*): the greeting and a list to change it, applied
+  at once. One per session (`$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/flickos/hello.lock`).
+- **History:** every change is recorded (`record()`) and shown in *Settings →
+  History*, which undoes it with `greeting set OLD`.
+- **A Recommends of `flickos-desktop`:** an app users may remove. It is in
+  new installs only; installed systems get it with `sudo apt install
+  flickos-hello`.
+- **Unit tests** in `tests/` (reading the files, the commands, History, one
+  window, no GTK for the commands, the shipped files), run at package build.
+  The boot test changes the greeting, undoes it from History and opens the
+  window (`boot-test/hello-dark.png`).
+
 ### `flickos-greeter`
 
 The login screen of installed systems: greetd runs gtkgreet in the cage kiosk
